{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1151751-2e-anchor-rules","id":1151751,"title":"[2E] Anchor Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-21T14:25:56-07:00","id":1151751,"title":"[2E] Anchor Rules","content":"The &quot;Anchors&quot; section of the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook (page 73) says the following in paragraph 2: &quot; If the Storyteller judges that your character's actions during a scene reflect his Vice, he regains one spent Willpower point. Note that acting on a Virtue or Vice does not need to pose difficulty or risk to your character.&quot; In paragraph 3, though, it says: &quot;If the storyteller judges that your character's actions during a scene reflected her Virtue while posing her difficulty or risk, she regains all spent Willpower.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is confusing. I can see two interpretations; one is that the first sentence of paragraph 2 should say &quot;Virtue OR Vice&quot; for one willpower point, or the second sentence of paragraph 2 should NOT say &quot;Virtue or Vice&quot;, just Vice. The latter is how I've understood the game to work up to this point. There's no listed mechanism for Virtues providing 1 willpower at no risk, so the second sentence of paragraph 2 shouldn't mention Virtues at all, it seems.<br /> <br /> Checking the equivalent section in the God-Machine Rules Update, it says that acting on your Vice doesn't need risk or difficulty, but the Virtue refresh does. But then the relevant section in Vampire: The Requiem 2nd edition, no mention of risk or difficulty, just &quot;meaningful action&quot; for the Virtue refresh. The same is true in Mage: The Awakening 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> So what's the deal? Is it meaningful actions? Difficulty or risk? Can you get 1WP from acting on your Virtue, and then all of them if you do so at risk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":".  why is my text invisible 10-21-2017, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T17:28:35-07:00","id":1153840,"title":"","content":"The way I understand paragraph 2 is: &quot;You can always act on a Virtue Or a Vice even when there is no diffuculty/risk for the character to do so. However, acting on a Virtue when there is no risk will not allow you to regain a Willpower Point, but acting on a Vice will (at the ST discretion).&quot;<br /> <br /> Paragraph 3 complete the loop by adding: &quot;If however there was a risk or difficulty involved when you played your Virtue, you are allowed to regain a Willpower Point again at the ST discretion.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a